WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.385
Rishi’s dad tried to calm Babu Yadav, but he was still upset.

2
00:00:06.386 --> 00:00:10.490
"He tried to hurt my cow," Babu Yadav said.

3
00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.449
"It is wrong."

4
00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.275
"What did I do?" cried Vinnie, worried.

5
00:00:18.276 --> 00:00:23.353
"Babu Yadav, I give you my word," said Rishi’s father.

6
00:00:23.354 --> 00:00:26.833
"I will bring the boy to the king myself."

7
00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:32.194
"You’d better take him to the king!" Babu Yadav threatened.

8
00:00:32.195 --> 00:00:34.818
He left with the cow.

9
00:00:34.819 --> 00:00:39.609
"Why are cows so important?" asked Mandy.

10
00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:44.223
"The cow is like our mother," began Rishi’s father.

11
00:00:44.224 --> 00:00:48.429
"I don’t understand," said Mandy.

12
00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:55.796
"Cows are gentle creatures and provide milk to feed the world," Rishi’s father continued.

13
00:00:55.797 --> 00:00:58.752
"It would be wrong to harm your mother."

14
00:00:58.753 --> 00:01:03.031
"Why do I have to see the king?" asked Vinnie.

15
00:01:03.032 --> 00:01:07.707
"Babu Yadav insists," said Rishi’s father.

16
00:01:07.708 --> 00:01:10.422
"We have to go to the palace.

17
00:01:10.423 --> 00:01:13.545
The king will decide what is best."

18
00:01:13.546 --> 00:01:17.169
Rima and her mother stayed home.

19
00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:21.653
Vinnie and Mandy left with Rishi and his father.

20
00:01:21.654 --> 00:01:24.956
They walked down the muddy roads.

21
00:01:24.957 --> 00:01:30.058
Vinnie noticed many cows walking around freely.

22
00:01:30.059 --> 00:01:33.829
"Do you believe in karma?" asked Rishi.

23
00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:37.506
"What’s karma?" asked Vinnie.

24
00:01:37.507 --> 00:01:41.049
"Our bodies die, but our souls do not.

25
00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:44.768
We live many lives," said Rishi.

26
00:01:44.769 --> 00:01:50.554
"If we hurt an animal or a person, we will be hurt in our next life."

27
00:01:50.555 --> 00:01:56.843
Rishi continued, "This is why all living things should be treated kindly."

28
00:01:56.844 --> 00:02:00.738
Suddenly, they heard a loud clapping noise.

29
00:02:00.739 --> 00:02:04.471
People on the road moved to the side.

30
00:02:04.472 --> 00:02:08.795
Everyone stood still covering their eyes.

31
00:02:08.796 --> 00:02:11.728
"What’s up?" asked Vinnie.

32
00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:15.602
"Do not look!" Rishi said urgently.

33
00:02:15.603 --> 00:02:19.832
An old man in torn clothes walked up the road.

34
00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:23.838
He was clapping two wooden boards together.

35
00:02:23.839 --> 00:02:28.181
"Hello," Mandy called out to him softly.

36
00:02:28.182 --> 00:02:32.353
The man turned away from Mandy and kept walking.

37
00:02:32.354 --> 00:02:37.662
After he left, Rishi and the others started on their way again.

38
00:02:37.663 --> 00:02:42.943
"Why didn’t anyone look at him?" Mandy asked Rishi.

39
00:02:42.944 --> 00:02:47.097
"He’s an untouchable," explained Rishi.

40
00:02:47.098 --> 00:02:51.848
"Why was he clapping those wooden things?" asked Vinnie.

41
00:02:51.849 --> 00:02:53.242
"It’s the law.

42
00:02:53.243 --> 00:02:59.061
Untouchables must alert everyone that they are coming," Rishi replied.

43
00:02:59.062 --> 00:03:02.442
"No one is supposed to even look at them.

44
00:03:02.443 --> 00:03:05.497
They are the lowest kind of people.

45
00:03:05.498 --> 00:03:09.313
Untouchables do the dirtiest jobs."

46
00:03:09.314 --> 00:03:12.624
"Why?" said Mandy.

47
00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:17.361
"We have castes in our society," Rishi began.

48
00:03:17.362 --> 00:03:22.610
He pointed to two men with their hair knotted on top of their heads.

49
00:03:22.611 --> 00:03:26.401
"They are the highest caste, the Brahmans.

50
00:03:26.402 --> 00:03:29.919
They are our religious teachers."

51
00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:35.629
A large elephant with bells came in the opposite direction.

52
00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:39.996
On its back was a colorful rug and carriage.

53
00:03:39.997 --> 00:03:43.456
A young man in white sat on top.

54
00:03:43.457 --> 00:03:46.830
"The nobles are the next highest caste.

55
00:03:46.831 --> 00:03:49.717
Like him," said Rishi.

56
00:03:49.718 --> 00:03:54.042
"The next caste is made up of farmers and merchants.

57
00:03:54.043 --> 00:03:59.090
My family belongs to this caste," Rishi said proudly.

58
00:03:59.091 --> 00:04:04.604
"Below us are the servants’ caste and finally the untouchables."

59
00:04:04.605 --> 00:04:09.590
Mandy and Vinnie just looked at each other.

